  "cleanup": "Disposable VMs, containers, sockets, initramfs and snapshot disks removed. One cached tool image remains for fast reruns. Superseded C probe and its compiler dependency removed. No host was paused or reconfigured.",
  "limits": [
    "BootClock is test-only. The CLI is not switched and no production physical timing profile is selected.",
    "The 1 ms allowance is an experimental threshold, not an established platform-wide bound. Host/guest interval sampling includes serial transport.",
    "Owner restore uses the native Rust owner, journal, recovery and provider HTTP binding. The object store fixture and successor run on the host, outside restored guest memory. This does not test a cloud service or the public HTTP router.",
    "The binding checks PID before touching inherited state, then checks the VMClock marker and current tsc clocksource before and after time sampling. Timeline retirement survives later valid readings.",
    "QEMU 10.1.5 behavior does not establish every hypervisor contract. The raw kvm-clock sample still misses a QMP pause; the binding now rejects that source before ownership can begin.",
    "Cross-host rate/error bounds, live migration, frequency changes, hardware suspend, PID namespace recreation, CRIU, VM cloning and repeated combined faults remain unqualified. A privileged switch away from tsc and back between samples is outside this candidate contract.",
    "No new protocol theorem or Rust refinement is claimed. The existing conditional timing contract and failure retirement path are unchanged.",
    "Short guest ACPI suspend is now an observed counterexample, not merely an untested obligation. Larger timing margins and post-resume statistics have not been adopted as a fix."
  ],
